# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data stays on your machine.
#
# Every folder that holds source data is ignored by default, and only its
# README is tracked. This is deliberate. Survey exports, keyword pulls,
# analytics downloads, and licensed third-party research do not belong in a
# public repository, and git history keeps them even after a delete.
#
# If you want a file tracked, add it explicitly: git add -f <path>
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

**/customer_data/**
!**/customer_data/README.md

**/keyword_data/**
!**/keyword_data/README.md

**/search_console/**
!**/search_console/README.md

**/analytics_data/**
!**/analytics_data/README.md

# The working area. Outputs are disposable by design.
99_Outputs/**
!99_Outputs/README.md

# Common data formats, anywhere in the tree
*.csv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.zip
*.pdf

# Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
credentials.*
secrets.*

# OS and editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
